# Content packs (All-In-One)

Uni+ Learning Tools reads **only** `content-packs/` through content-api. A pack appears when this file exists:

`content-packs/<pack-folder>/manifest.json`

Do **not** nest packs in `S1/` / `S3/` or any year folder. Do **not** add teaching files under `dashboard/`, `slides/`, `media/`, `public/`, or `dist/` (old hub).

## Folder shape (one lesson = one pack)

```
content-packs/jm24-law-of-indices/
  manifest.json
  tools/<slug>/index.html
  tools/shared/
  concepts/<topicId>/
  quiz/
```

## New lesson

1. Copy an existing pack folder. Rename it (`jm36-…`).
2. In `manifest.json`: `subject` `"MATH"`, unique lowercase `scope`, `chapterCode`, `published: true`.
3. List every tool, game, quiz, comic, summary, and concept video. Unlisted files are invisible.
4. Tag items with a syllabus **Symbol** from `content/topics/math-topics.json` (`Index`, `MFact`). Do not invent Symbols.

## Quizzes

Edit `quiz/<id>/questions.json` in that pack. Keep old `id` values; new items get new ids. List the quiz in `manifest.json`. Leave quiz runners, `postMessage`, and tracking unchanged.

All-In-One renders stems through KaTeX. Write the JSON for that renderer — do not add special cases in Uni+ TypeScript.

- Math goes in `$…$` (or `\(` `\)`). Bare `\ge`, `\frac`, `x^{2}` will not render once a `$` is also in the string.
- Line breaks are real JSON newlines, never the two characters `\n`.
- Money is `\$30 000`, not `$30 000` (a bare `$` starts math).
- After editing, run `bun --cwd content-packs run lint:quizzes` from this repo.

## HTML to keep

`content-packs/<pack>/tools/<slug>/index.html` (and its JS/CSS) — All-In-One embeds this.

## Stop

Duplicate `scope`, year-folder wrappers, or quiz runner / tracking changes → ask the technical owner. Do not push.
